## 6. Entity Mapping Optimization

**❌ NEVER: Use default eager loading**

```java
// BAD: Loads ALL orders for every customer query — N+1 problem
@OneToMany(fetch = FetchType.EAGER)
private List<Order> orders;
```

**✅ ALWAYS: Default to LAZY, fetch explicitly when needed**

```java
// GOOD: Only loads orders when explicitly accessed or JOIN FETCH'd
@OneToMany(fetch = FetchType.LAZY, mappedBy = "customer")
private Set<Order> orders;  // Use Set, not List, for @ManyToMany

// In JPQL: load the association when needed
@Query("SELECT c FROM Customer c JOIN FETCH c.orders WHERE c.id = :id")
Optional<Customer> findWithOrders(@Param("id") UUID id);
```

**Additional optimizations:**

```java
// Use DynamicUpdate for entities with many nullable columns
@Entity
@DynamicUpdate  // Only SET columns that actually changed
@DynamicInsert  // Only INSERT non-null columns
public class LargeEntity { ... }

// Use getById() (reference proxy) instead of findById() when you only need the FK
Customer customer = customerRepository.getById(customerId);  // No SELECT issued
order.setCustomer(customer);  // Sets FK without loading Customer

// Use @Immutable for read-only entities (disables dirty checking)
@Entity
@Immutable
public class AuditLogEntry { ... }
```

**❌ NEVER: Use Open-Session-In-View (OSIV)**

```properties
# BAD: Keeps Hibernate session open during HTTP response rendering
# Causes lazy loading in the view layer = unpredictable N+1 queries
spring.jpa.open-in-view=true  # ❌ NEVER

# GOOD: Disable OSIV, fetch everything you need in the service layer
spring.jpa.open-in-view=false  # ✅ ALWAYS
```

