## 7. Transaction Scope Management

**❌ NEVER: Call external APIs inside a database transaction**

```java
// BAD: HTTP call holds the transaction open for 200-2000ms
@Transactional
public void processOrder(UUID orderId) {
    Order order = orderRepo.findById(orderId).orElseThrow();
    PaymentResult result = paymentGateway.charge(order.getAmount());  // ❌ 200ms HTTP call
    order.setPaymentId(result.id());
    order.setStatus("PAID");
    orderRepo.save(order);
}
```

**✅ ALWAYS: Separate external calls from transactions**

```java
public void processOrder(UUID orderId) {
    // 1. Read (can use AS OF SYSTEM TIME for staleness-tolerant reads)
    Order order = orderRepo.findById(orderId).orElseThrow();

    // 2. External call OUTSIDE transaction
    PaymentResult result = paymentGateway.charge(order.getAmount());

    // 3. Short write transaction
    updateOrderPayment(orderId, result.id());
}

@Transactional
public void updateOrderPayment(UUID orderId, String paymentId) {
    orderRepo.updatePayment(orderId, paymentId, "PAID");
}
```

**Read-only transactions:**

```java
// For read-only operations, mark as read-only to avoid write overhead
@Transactional(readOnly = true)
public List<Order> getRecentOrders(UUID customerId) {
    return orderRepo.findByCustomerIdOrderByCreatedAtDesc(customerId);
}
```

