## 8. Query Parallelism for Bulk DML

When batch DML exceeds 250K-500K rows:

```java
// GOOD: Parallel threads on DISJOINTED key ranges (never overlapping)
// 4 threads on 7M rows: ~2 minutes vs single-threaded timeouts with retries

// Step 1: Read key boundaries in a read-only transaction
List<UUID> boundaries = jdbcTemplate.queryForList(
    "SELECT id FROM large_table ORDER BY id", UUID.class);

// Step 2: Partition into N non-overlapping ranges
List<Range> ranges = partitionIntoRanges(boundaries, 4);

// Step 3: Fan out parallel DML — each thread uses implicit transactions
ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(4);
ranges.forEach(range -> pool.submit(() -> {
    jdbcTemplate.update(
        "DELETE FROM large_table WHERE id >= ? AND id < ?",
        range.start(), range.end());
}));
```

**Rules:**
- NEVER overlap key ranges between threads (causes 40001 serialization failures)
- Use implicit transactions per batch (no explicit BEGIN/COMMIT)
- Run during maintenance windows with sufficient CPU/memory headroom
- For operations requiring atomicity across tables, use CTE-based set operations instead

