## 9. Migration from PostgreSQL/Oracle Checklist

| PostgreSQL/Oracle Pattern | CockroachDB Replacement |
|--------------------------|------------------------|
| `SERIAL` / `BIGSERIAL` / `AUTO_INCREMENT` | `UUID DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()` |
| Stored procedures with loops | CTE-based set operations |
| `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` (queue pattern) | Retry-based concurrency or partitioned queue |
| Transactional DDL (multiple ALTERs in BEGIN) | One DDL per implicit transaction |
| `PL/pgSQL` cursors for row-by-row processing | Set-based CTEs or application-tier batch |
| Oracle sequences for PK generation | UUID or Hi-Lo batched sequence with allocationSize=50 |
| `COPY` for bulk load | `IMPORT INTO` for large datasets, `COPY FROM` for moderate |
| pg_dump for backup | `BACKUP INTO` (CockroachDB native) |
| Use MOLT tools (Schema Conversion Tool, Fetch, Verify) for migration |

